WEBVTT

00:03.260 --> 00:08.550
A drifting place for lonely women～♪

00:08.550 --> 00:10.220
Mr. Reiji.

00:10.220 --> 00:12.170
This isn't like you at all.

00:12.170 --> 00:14.440
Are you still thinking about Tomomi?

00:14.440 --> 00:17.300
I guess I've always been nothing but a droopy-eared stuffed animal.

00:17.300 --> 00:19.330
Please don't say that.

00:19.330 --> 00:22.280
The new applicants are ready for you now.

00:22.850 --> 00:26.560
Maybe I'll try going north this time.

00:27.030 --> 00:28.460
Hi, I'm Gyo.

00:28.460 --> 00:31.870
I can drink booze all night long just like you,

00:31.870 --> 00:36.890
so I figured, "why not get a job which pays me to drink and flirt with hotties like Mr. Reiji"?

00:35.230 --> 00:37.520
If you're jealous of what I have here,

00:37.520 --> 00:40.680
you'd better also be jealous of all the hard work I did to get here.

00:40.680 --> 00:41.850
Hi, I'm Khamenman.

00:41.850 --> 00:44.350
I heard girls these days liked old guys, so I—

00:44.350 --> 00:45.540
They like <i>old </i>, not <i>ancient </i>.

00:45.540 --> 00:46.610
Devilcat here.

00:46.610 --> 00:49.700
My doctor said I should try developing a relatively stable daily routine,

00:49.700 --> 00:51.240
so I want to get a job which lets me work from nine to five!

00:51.240 --> 00:52.500
Get lost.

00:52.500 --> 00:53.480
I'm sorry.

00:53.480 --> 00:56.260
I'll bring in one more applicant next week.

00:56.260 --> 00:58.640
There is only one person...

00:58.640 --> 01:00.600
who could possibly surpass me.

01:00.600 --> 01:02.560
Come quickly,

01:02.560 --> 01:03.340
Usa.

01:03.340 --> 01:04.920
Droopy Ears!

01:04.920 --> 01:07.670
I've got another favor to ask!

01:08.390 --> 01:09.470
What's going on?

01:08.390 --> 01:09.470
He's so cute!

01:09.470 --> 01:12.410
That's ten bottles of Dom Pérignon for Mr. Usacots!

01:12.410 --> 01:14.550
Thank you for your patronage!

02:51.130 --> 02:52.860
Are you making sātā andāgī?

02:52.860 --> 02:55.000
I sure am.

02:55.000 --> 02:57.240
I love sātā andāgī!

02:57.640 --> 03:01.190
Sātā andāgī are good, aren't they?

03:01.650 --> 03:03.510
Red's on the line for you, Master Vamp.

03:04.200 --> 03:06.210
Why does he have to call when I'm busy?

03:07.210 --> 03:08.840
Hello?

03:08.840 --> 03:10.420
Um, Mr. Red?

03:10.420 --> 03:13.920
I'm sorry, but could you call back in five minutes?

03:13.920 --> 03:15.900
I'm making sātā andāgī right now—

03:15.900 --> 03:18.960
I'll kick your ass if you keep blabbering nonsense like that.

03:18.960 --> 03:21.520
What are you making now?

03:21.520 --> 03:22.650
Well,

03:22.650 --> 03:26.080
I was making sātā andāgī; they're Okinawa-style donuts.

03:26.080 --> 03:27.280
Kill the fire for me.

03:27.280 --> 03:27.780
Yes, sir.

03:27.780 --> 03:29.080
Are you listening to what I'm saying?

03:29.080 --> 03:30.850
Yes, I can talk now.

03:30.850 --> 03:32.610
So, what can I do you for?

03:32.610 --> 03:34.090
Let me ask you something:

03:34.090 --> 03:37.470
are you guys planning on attacking me on the 26th?

03:38.470 --> 03:40.410
The 26th?

03:42.160 --> 03:45.600
Oh, we're going to the Super Bathhouse that day,

03:45.600 --> 03:47.580
so we were going to completely ignore yo—

03:47.580 --> 03:50.030
I mean, no, we're not planning to attack you that day.

03:50.030 --> 03:52.510
You sure better not be lying to me.

03:52.510 --> 03:56.610
I'll beat you up ten times worse than usual if you attack me that day.

03:56.610 --> 03:57.980
I understand, okay.

03:58.680 --> 04:01.760
Are you doing something on the 26th?

04:01.760 --> 04:04.450
That's none of your freakin' business.

04:04.850 --> 04:07.880
Don't you dare attack me that day, got it?

04:07.880 --> 04:08.880
Don't you dare!

04:13.880 --> 04:16.750
God damn it, even after all that I said...

04:16.750 --> 04:18.860
Is your brain made out of crab guts or something?

04:18.860 --> 04:19.900
Well, <i>he's </i> an octopus—

04:19.900 --> 04:21.860
That's not the point!

04:21.860 --> 04:24.250
You just had to attack when I'm busy.

04:24.250 --> 04:27.680
I thought I told you over the phone <i>not </i> to attack me on the 26th!

04:27.680 --> 04:30.830
I wasn't planning on it either.

04:30.830 --> 04:32.430
I wasn't planning on it,

04:32.430 --> 04:35.730
but you were so insistent on telling us <i>not </i> to attack you,

04:35.730 --> 04:37.730
so I thought maybe you were trying to tell us <i>to </i> attack.

04:37.730 --> 04:39.840
You think I'm trying to be funny here?

04:39.840 --> 04:43.090
Why are you trying to make it sound like it's my fault?

04:43.090 --> 04:45.360
You're going to get wrinkles on your jacket...

04:44.360 --> 04:46.960
That's exactly why I told you not to attack!

04:49.440 --> 04:50.900
Go to hell, Red!

04:50.900 --> 04:52.600
Shut up!

04:53.240 --> 04:54.080
You punk!

04:54.080 --> 04:55.560
What are you spraying ink at me for?

04:55.560 --> 04:56.610
You need to use rice grains to get the ink out.

04:56.610 --> 04:57.970
else it's going to stain—

04:57.970 --> 05:00.210
Rice grains this, you punk bitch!

05:00.210 --> 05:01.970
Ow...

05:01.970 --> 05:03.470
It might take a little time,

05:03.470 --> 05:05.940
but that's the best way to remove the stain.

05:05.940 --> 05:09.050
You punks think this is all a big joke...

05:09.050 --> 05:11.390
Oh crap, I'm running out of time.

05:11.390 --> 05:12.880
I gotta hurry over and pick her up.

05:12.880 --> 05:14.980
Who are you picking up?

05:14.980 --> 05:18.400
Kayoko's mother is visiting from the countryside.

05:18.400 --> 05:21.340
Kayoko's at work so I gotta go pick her up instead.

05:22.510 --> 05:24.670
Kayoko's mother, you say?

05:28.360 --> 05:29.620
They look so good!

05:29.620 --> 05:31.320
Go on, help yourselves.

05:31.620 --> 05:33.850
I made two types of sātā andāgī;

05:33.850 --> 05:36.510
one's got black sugar, and the other has white sugar.

05:36.510 --> 05:37.780
That's awesome!

05:37.780 --> 05:39.460
Let's give one to Mr. Red too,

05:39.460 --> 05:41.960
since he doesn't seem to know what they are.

05:41.960 --> 05:43.000
Which one are you going to give him?

05:43.000 --> 05:46.350
I'll let him try the black sugar one, since it's richer in flavor.

05:46.350 --> 05:47.890
Mr. Red—

05:48.900 --> 05:51.120
The sātā andāgī...

05:51.720 --> 05:53.590
My sātā andāgī...

05:54.150 --> 05:56.130
I'm so sorry, Mr. Red,

05:56.130 --> 05:57.940
I'll get you a new one right now.

05:57.940 --> 05:59.570
Oh how clumsy of me.

05:59.570 --> 06:02.960
Just follow that donut all the way to Okinawa, won't you?

06:03.260 --> 06:06.090
Why the hell are you guys here anyway?

06:06.490 --> 06:08.130
Isn't it obvious?

06:08.130 --> 06:09.850
We want to meet Kayoko's mother too.

06:09.850 --> 06:10.890
Why?

06:11.190 --> 06:14.810
Well she's the mother of a friend who's done so much for us...

06:14.810 --> 06:16.980
You should really re-evaluate that way of thinking

06:16.980 --> 06:19.530
and judge whether that kind of thinking is suitable for an evil organization or not.

06:19.530 --> 06:20.740
Master Vamp?

06:20.740 --> 06:21.740
What is it, Number One?

06:21.740 --> 06:23.710
I think we should go back.

06:23.710 --> 06:25.020
But why?

06:25.020 --> 06:28.270
I want to meet Kayoko's mother too, you know.

06:28.270 --> 06:31.740
Let's let Red keep at least some of his dignity today.

06:31.740 --> 06:33.700
It looks like he's meeting her mother for the first time

06:33.700 --> 06:37.040
since he's all dressed up.

06:37.040 --> 06:39.870
Don't you think Mr. Red might be feeling a bit insecure, then?

06:39.870 --> 06:42.030
I think it'd be better for us to stay with him.

06:42.030 --> 06:44.230
He's got his pride to keep as Kayoko's boyfriend.

06:44.230 --> 06:45.080
He actually has some?

06:45.080 --> 06:47.780
He wants to meet her mother before you do, Master Vamp.

06:47.780 --> 06:49.960
R-Really?

06:50.890 --> 06:52.180
Oh yeah,

06:52.180 --> 06:54.280
I forgot I need to buy some meat and—

06:54.280 --> 06:55.140
Ow!

06:55.140 --> 06:55.940
head on home—

06:55.940 --> 06:56.600
Ow!

06:56.600 --> 06:57.980
so if you'll excuse me I'll be—

06:57.980 --> 06:58.280
Ow!

06:58.280 --> 06:58.770
Wait a—

06:58.770 --> 06:59.270
Ow!

06:59.270 --> 07:01.260
Seriously, that one really hurt—

07:01.260 --> 07:01.750
Ow!

07:01.750 --> 07:03.860
I think we should get going, guys.

07:09.850 --> 07:11.750
I want to get married!

07:09.850 --> 07:11.750
[kɛkkɔnˈ ʃɪtɑɪˈ]

07:15.070 --> 07:17.090
Wasn't there a detective show on today?

07:17.900 --> 07:20.230
Blood stains and corpses!

07:17.900 --> 07:20.230
[kɛkˈkɔn ʃɪˈtɑɪ]

07:21.320 --> 07:23.210
This place is covered with blood stains as well.

07:32.200 --> 07:36.700
Hellwolf has been waiting over thirty minutes for his ramen.

07:37.300 --> 07:39.000
I'm sorry it took so long.

07:39.000 --> 07:40.810
I kill youz!

07:40.810 --> 07:43.720
We upgraded your order to BBQ Pork ramen to compensate...

07:45.380 --> 07:46.600
I... love youz!

07:46.600 --> 07:47.280
I... love youz!

07:52.760 --> 07:54.860
Can you give me 300 grams of pork belly?

07:54.860 --> 07:55.860
Sure.

07:55.860 --> 07:58.050
They got croquettes on sale, Master Vamp!

07:58.050 --> 07:59.590
I guess we'll get those too, then.

07:59.590 --> 08:00.480
Yay!

08:10.310 --> 08:11.570
Damn it.

08:14.160 --> 08:16.930
You know our company expenses can't cover that.

08:16.930 --> 08:18.120
I'm sorry though.

08:18.120 --> 08:19.150
At least I tried.

08:19.150 --> 08:20.500
You really got it going on, don't you, Number Two?

08:22.790 --> 08:24.370
Isn't that Red?

08:24.370 --> 08:25.350
He's still there.

08:25.350 --> 08:28.150
It's been over an hour since we left him.

08:28.450 --> 08:29.670
Mr. Red!

08:30.670 --> 08:32.280
Have you not met her yet?

08:32.280 --> 08:33.870
It's you guys again.

08:34.310 --> 08:36.510
She was supposed to be here at three thirty.

08:37.010 --> 08:39.840
That can't be right.

08:39.840 --> 08:41.190
You bought your meat, didn't you?

08:41.190 --> 08:42.580
Don't you have to go home now?

08:43.080 --> 08:44.000
Oh don't worry.

08:44.000 --> 08:44.950
It's cold out today,

08:44.950 --> 08:48.770
plus I bought frozen giblets as well, so it should be nice and cold inside the bag—

08:48.770 --> 08:52.570
Do you really think I give a crap about your meat?

08:52.570 --> 08:54.310
Hey Mr. Red, look at that person!

08:54.850 --> 08:57.040
Doesn't she look like Kayoko?

08:57.040 --> 09:00.600
That could be her mom; she looks like she's been waiting for someone.

09:00.600 --> 09:03.200
Now that you mention it, she <i>has </i> been there for a while

09:03.600 --> 09:04.870
You think she looks like Kayoko?

09:04.870 --> 09:06.370
Of course she does!

09:06.370 --> 09:08.590
She has Kayoko's eyes!

09:08.590 --> 09:10.550
Now that you mention it, her nose looks like Kayoko's too.

09:10.550 --> 09:11.380
Her mouth too.

09:11.380 --> 09:13.130
That's got to be her mother!

09:13.130 --> 09:15.360
What have you been doing all this time?

09:15.360 --> 09:18.090
You should go talk to her right now.

09:18.090 --> 09:19.050
You sure about that?

09:19.050 --> 09:20.270
Come on!

09:28.870 --> 09:30.190
Thank goodness.

09:30.190 --> 09:32.060
Amen to that.

09:33.390 --> 09:34.850
See? What did I tell you—

09:34.850 --> 09:36.120
That wasn't her!

09:36.620 --> 09:37.710
Wait a second!

09:37.710 --> 09:39.800
The Nambu line has other stations that start with "Musashi"

09:39.800 --> 09:44.030
like "Musashi-Shinjo", "Musashi-Nakahara", and "Musashi-Kosugi," right?

09:44.550 --> 09:47.380
Maybe she got off the wrong stop.

09:47.920 --> 09:49.270
You could be right.

09:49.270 --> 09:49.950
Mr. Red!

09:49.950 --> 09:53.320
Can you just go to that Super Bathhouse or wherever you were supposed go?

09:53.320 --> 09:55.330
Why don't you give Kayoko a call?

09:55.330 --> 09:58.090
There's a chance that she might know something about it.

09:58.090 --> 10:00.210
Didn't I tell you she's at work?

10:00.210 --> 10:02.010
Just a moment, please.

10:04.400 --> 10:05.910
Hello? Kayoko?

10:05.910 --> 10:06.740
It's me.

10:06.740 --> 10:08.860
Why the hell do you know her number?

10:08.860 --> 10:10.720
Yeah, I'm with Mr. Red right now.

10:10.720 --> 10:11.770
Do you want to talk to him?

10:12.870 --> 10:14.020
It's me.

10:14.020 --> 10:15.110
I'm so sorry!

10:15.110 --> 10:16.290
I meant to call,

10:16.290 --> 10:20.050
but you don't have a cellphone so I had to wait for you to call.

10:20.050 --> 10:22.870
Thank god Vamp's there with you.

10:23.720 --> 10:24.980
So yeah,

10:24.980 --> 10:27.620
I haven't exactly met your mother yet.

10:33.730 --> 10:35.460
Okay.

10:37.140 --> 10:38.410
Bye then.

10:38.780 --> 10:39.630
How do you hang up?

10:40.130 --> 10:41.280
I'll do it for—

10:41.280 --> 10:42.030
Ow!

10:42.030 --> 10:44.060
Apparently Kayoko's sister called from Tokyo...

10:44.060 --> 10:45.110
Her sister?

10:45.110 --> 10:49.120
...and said that her mother will stay at her sister's place instead.

10:49.120 --> 10:51.710
I see.

10:52.620 --> 10:54.080
All right!

10:54.080 --> 10:56.210
Let's go drink, you guys.

11:00.320 --> 11:02.310
I'll say it now,

11:02.310 --> 11:06.240
but you have no idea how nervous I was about meeting Kayoko's mother.

11:06.240 --> 11:08.100
One more beer, old man.

11:08.100 --> 11:09.520
Coming up!

11:10.540 --> 11:12.900
You've already said that three times.

11:12.900 --> 11:15.600
I guess it'd be hard to meet her mother given the current circumstances.

11:15.600 --> 11:17.080
It's pretty complicated.

11:17.080 --> 11:18.120
All right!

11:18.120 --> 11:20.240
On to the next bar!

11:21.620 --> 11:22.890
Hold on a minute, Mr. Red!

11:22.890 --> 11:24.550
Astro Fighter Sunred.

11:24.550 --> 11:27.490
This is the story of the conflict between good and evil

11:27.490 --> 11:29.950
that takes place in the city of Kawasaki.
